1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,030
Thank you for calling the Tourist Line.

2
00:00:03,030 --> 00:00:06,021
There are many different ways of getting round the city

3
00:00:06,021 --> 00:00:09,610
and we'd like to suggest some you may not have thought of.

4
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:12,740
How about a city trip by boat?

5
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:19,113
There are four main stopping points from west to east:

6
00:00:19,113 --> 00:00:29,310
stop A Green Banks, stop B City Bridge, stop C Roman Landing and stop D Newtown.

7
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:33,960
You can find the main booking office at stop A.

8
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:40,550
The first boat leaves at 8 a. m. and the last one at 6.30 p. m.

9
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:45,230
There are also many attractions you can visit along the river.

10
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:48,363
At Stop A, if you have time,

11
00:00:48,363 --> 00:00:56,420
you can visit the fine 16th century palace here built for the king with its beautiful formal gardens.

12
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:58,870
It's very near the booking office.

13
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:03,740
Now you can enjoy every corner of this superb residence.

14
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:11,030
Stop B Why don't you visit Tower Restaurant with its wide range of refreshments?

15
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:13,715
This is a place where you can sit

16
00:01:13,715 --> 00:01:16,840
and enjoy the wonderful views over the old commercial

17
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:18,750
and banking centre of the city.

18
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:24,860
Stop C is the area where, in the first century AD

19
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:26,350
invading soldiers crossed the river;

20
00:01:26,350 --> 00:01:30,150
this was much shallower than it is now.

21
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:34,080
That's why this area is called Roman Landing.

22
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:39,280
There's an interactive Museum to visit here with a large shop

23
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:42,140
which has a good range of local history books.

24
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:46,337
At the furthest point of the trip, stop D,

25
00:01:46,979 --> 00:01:51,678
the most exciting place to visit is the new Entertainment Complex

26
00:01:51,678 --> 00:01:55,970
with seven-screen cinema, bowling alley and video games arcade.

27
00:01:55,970 --> 00:02:00,430
Besides the boat tours, there are city buses.

28
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:02,869
Two companies offer special services:

29
00:02:02,869 --> 00:02:09,700
The Top Bus Company runs all its tours with a live commentary in English.

30
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:15,170
Tours leave from 8.30 a. m. every 20 minutes.

31
00:02:15,170 --> 00:02:22,050
There are departures from Central Station, Castle Hill and Long Walk.

32
00:02:22,050 --> 00:02:29,000
This is a hop-on hop-off service and tickets are valid for 24 hours.

33
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:39,080
For further details call Top Bus on 0208 9447810.

34
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:46,630
The Number One Sightseeing Tour is available with a commentary in eight languages.

35
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:53,298
Buses depart from Central Station every five to six minutes from about 9 a.

36
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:58,060
m. with the last bus at around 7 p. m.

37
00:02:58,060 --> 00:03:03,660
There are also Number One services with an English-speaking...
